IMPORT prelude

-- Air Accidents (Commonwealth Government Liability) Act 1963 (Cth) — THE
-- NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL. Source:
-- ../registers/source-bundle/C1963A00074.txt (compilation No. 9, 17 June
-- 2021). The passenger hurt in an air accident, or their dependants, ask:
-- "Is the Commonwealth liable under this Act; how much can be recovered; is
-- my claim barred or on hold?"

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Operator` IS ONE OF
    `the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority`
    `another operator`

-- s 11(1), (3A), (4): why the Commonwealth (or the ACT or NT) is connected
-- with the carriage.
DECLARE `Connection` IS ONE OF
    `a Commonwealth employee or seaman travelling in the course of employment`
    `the Commonwealth or an authority bears the cost of carriage`
    `travelling for Commonwealth purposes under its arrangements`
    `the same connection with the ACT or the Northern Territory`
    `none`

DECLARE `Air case` HAS
    `the operator`                                                  IS A `Operator`
    -- s 4 passenger
    `I was on board as working crew of a commercial operator`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the connection`                                                IS A `Connection`
    -- ss 6(1), 11(2)
    `Part IV of the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1959 or a declared State Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 6(2), 11(3)
    `the death or injury entitles someone to a Veterans' Entitlements pension` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 12
    `the accident was on board or in embarking or disembarking`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 8(1), 14(1)
    `the s 31(1AA) amount`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `the s 31(1)(b) amount prescribed at the accident`              IS A NUMBER
    -- the damages otherwise assessed
    `the damages assessed`                                          IS A NUMBER
    -- ss 8(2), 14(2)
    `insurance received from the Commonwealth's cover or allowance` IS A NUMBER
    `damages or compensation from the carrier or others`            IS A NUMBER
    -- ss 10(1)(a), 15(1)(a)
    `I recovered damages from the Commonwealth otherwise than under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 16
    `I failed to pursue others I could reasonably have pursued`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I settled with another without the Commonwealth's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I refused the Commonwealth's request to sue another`           IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 17
    `an action against another is pending`                          IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Part` IS ONE OF
    `Part II`
    `Part III`
    `neither Part`

DECLARE `Air position` HAS
    `the Part that applies`                                         IS A `Part`
    `the maximum liability`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `the damages recoverable under this Act`                        IS A NUMBER
    `my action can be heard now`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- s 4 passenger: not crew employed by a commercial operator on board to work.
@ref s 4 passenger
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a passenger` c IF
    NOT (c's `I was on board as working crew of a commercial operator`)

-- s 6: Part II; s 11: Part III.
@ref ss 6, 11
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A `Part`
`the Part for` c MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`I am a passenger` c)
           OR c's `Part IV of the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act 1959 or a declared State Act applies`
           OR c's `the death or injury entitles someone to a Veterans' Entitlements pension`
            THEN `neither Part`
        IF c's `the operator` EQUALS `the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority` THEN `Part II`
        IF NOT (c's `the connection` EQUALS `none`) THEN `Part III`
        OTHERWISE `neither Part`

-- ss 8(1), 14(1): the s 31(1AA) amount, or a higher prescribed s 31(1)(b)
-- amount in force at the accident.
@ref ss 8(1), 14(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the cap for` c MEANS
    IF c's `the s 31(1)(b) amount prescribed at the accident` GREATER THAN c's `the s 31(1AA) amount`
    THEN c's `the s 31(1)(b) amount prescribed at the accident`
    ELSE c's `the s 31(1AA) amount`

-- ss 8(2), 14(2): deductions; s 14(2)(a) adds what the carrier and others pay.
@ref ss 8(2), 14(2)
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deductions for` c MEANS
    IF `the Part for` c EQUALS `Part III`
    THEN c's `insurance received from the Commonwealth's cover or allowance` PLUS c's `damages or compensation from the carrier or others`
    ELSE c's `insurance received from the Commonwealth's cover or allowance`

-- ss 10(1)(a), 15(1)(a), 16(1): no damages under this Part.
@ref ss 10(1)(a), 15(1)(a), 16(1)
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my damages are barred` c IF
        c's `I recovered damages from the Commonwealth otherwise than under this Act`
    OR  (    `the Part for` c EQUALS `Part III`
         AND (   c's `I failed to pursue others I could reasonably have pursued`
              OR c's `I settled with another without the Commonwealth's written consent`
              OR c's `I refused the Commonwealth's request to sue another`))

-- The damages assessed, capped (ss 8(1), 14(1)), less the deductions (ss 8(2),
-- 14(2)), not below nil. Part III requires an accident on board or in
-- embarking or disembarking (s 12).
@ref ss 8, 12, 14
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the damages for` c MEANS
    IF     `the Part for` c EQUALS `neither Part`
        OR `my damages are barred` c
        OR NOT (c's `the accident was on board or in embarking or disembarking`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF capped GREATER THAN `the deductions for` c THEN capped MINUS `the deductions for` c ELSE 0
    WHERE
        capped MEANS IF c's `the damages assessed` AT MOST `the cap for` c THEN c's `the damages assessed` ELSE `the cap for` c

-- s 17: not heard while an action against another is pending (Part III).
@ref s 17
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my action can be heard now` c IF
        `the damages for` c GREATER THAN 0
    AND NOT (`the Part for` c EQUALS `Part III` AND c's `an action against another is pending`)

@ref ss 4, 6, 8, 10-12, 14-17
@export default The position of a passenger killed or injured in an air accident, or their dependants, under the Air Accidents (Commonwealth Government Liability) Act 1963 (Cth): which Part applies (Part II for an aircraft operated by the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority; Part III for another operator where the passenger travelled for the Commonwealth, at its cost or as its employee, or likewise for the ACT or Northern Territory; neither where the Civil Aviation (Carriers' Liability) Act Part IV or a Veterans' Entitlements pension applies, or for working crew); the maximum liability (the Carriers' Liability Act amount, or a higher prescribed one); the damages recoverable after the Commonwealth-funded insurance and, under Part III, what the carrier and others pay; whether they are barred (damages recovered otherwise, or under Part III failing to pursue or settling with others or refusing the Commonwealth's request); and whether the action can be heard now (not while an action against another is pending). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Air case`  @desc The operator, my status and connection with the Commonwealth, the excluded regimes, the accident, the caps, the damages and deductions, and my dealings with others
GIVETH A `Air position`
`the air position for` c MEANS
    `Air position` OF `the Part for` c, `the cap for` c, `the damages for` c, `my action can be heard now` c
